# Wave W17-Q (Route 120): ledger pine — a long-rain pine in wet blue-greens, tiered like its rain-country kin but colder: the crown runs blue where Route 119’s gauge pine runs deep warm green, highlight lifted to the wet top, on ledger turf (ground baked in). Route 120’s own tree — the lake-and-cliff pine, split from the gauge pine by temperature (blue rain vs gorge rain) and from Yamato’s rain-country trees by the same cold register.
